 "_epoch_rationale": "Moons precess fast and orbit fast, so a long baseline ALIASES: the along-track error is 2*r*sin(delta/2), which folds at delta = 180 deg and returns to zero at 360 deg. Measured example: on the current tip Io is 6.13e5 km off at +180 d (delta = 266 deg) but a CORRECT propagator on the same data is 7.72e5 km off (delta = 133 deg) -- the wrong model scores better purely from the fold. Short baselines are where the position check has teeth; the long ones exist for the phase-immune plane check and for the slow precessors."
}
